// ============================================================================
// DEMO: replace_program()'s INTENDED use -- runtime polymorphism.
// This is the shared minimal base. See
// demo_poly_shell.lpc for the full pattern
// writeup and a map of the companion fixtures/tests.
// ============================================================================
//
// Bare-minimum, stateless scaffolding every monster needs regardless of
// concrete type -- deliberately carries NO variables of its own. Every
// concrete monster type (see demo_..._goblin/wolf/ghost.lpc) inherits
// this, and so does the shell (transitively, through each of the
// candidate types it inherits below) -- a real, stateful base would hit
// FluffOS's non-deduplicated diamond-inheritance behavior once inherited
// via more than one path, which is an orthogonal wrinkle this demo
// intentionally sidesteps (see testsuite/single/tests/efuns/
// replace_program_noop_generality.lpc's diamond-inheritance coverage for
// that topic on its own).
string base_marker() { return "base"; }

// Probe for /single/tests/efuns/replace_program_polymorphism_demo.lpc:
// living HERE (the one common ancestor, reached identically via all 3
// candidate paths -- see the shell's inherit list) means it resolves to
// the exact same function_t through every path, so it doesn't trip the
// diamond-inheritance function-conflict warnings the type-specific
// query_hp()/attack_damage()/hp do. Mirrors the try_bind() convention
// used throughout /clone/replace_program/replace_stateful_base.lpc and the shared
// /clone/replace_program/replace_min_target.lpc (used by the diamond/ml/vo generality
// axes): catch()ing a bound-args closure literal fails (nonzero) while a
// replace_program() swap is genuinely pending (make_lfun_funp() refuses
// to bind), and succeeds (0) once no swap is pending -- letting a caller
// directly observe whether replace_program_is_noop() correctly left this
// object's swap pending.
mixed try_bind() {
  mixed fp;
  return catch(fp = (: base_marker :));
}
